# RX (the numbered .in listing), FID (load by that number), LS (every file) in the manual's examples
# directory (cmdref: Session & Files).  The numbering is the directory's sorted order, so adding an example
# that sorts before CassWithExitPupil.in moves id 2 -- update the FID line then.
cd $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/examples
rx
fid
2
ls
# EXPECT: Listing Files in: \S+/docs/macos-manual/examples
# EXPECT: 1\s+AOExample\.in\s+2\s+CassWithExitPupil\.in\s+3\s+Cassegrain\.in
# EXPECT: Use FID command to load a Rx file\. Syntax: FID file_id
# EXPECT: Enter file id: \[1\]: 2\s+Input file CassWithExitPupil\.in\s+being loaded
# EXPECT: Tracing rays past\s+6 elements
# EXPECT: AOExample\.jou
# EXPECT-NOT: Invalid file id
# EXPECT-NOT: forrtl
